    "rules": {
      "intro": [
        "Captain {captain}. Welcome to the {base}, and to {client}.\n\nI'm Sabra Ollin, Road-Keeper of this fleet. We are Gyptians. Our grandmothers' grandmothers were the last to leave the Land, the world every human came from, and we have kept the road back in a book called the Reckoning. One day we will follow it home.\n\nPeople laugh at that. Let them. The Lantern Synod doesn't laugh. It even pays half your wages, which is why we can afford you.\n\nKit Farrow will fly your wing. Old Dov keeps the Reckoning. If he offers to show it to you, say yes. He doesn't offer often.",
        "So you're our new pilot. Good. I'm Sabra Ollin, and this ring is the {base}, the heart of our fleet.\n\nWe are the Gyptians. We say we come from Gyptian, the Land, the one world humans came from. Every gate we pass, we write down. Every gate is a step home, or a step away. Dov can tell you which, on a good day.\n\nWe have pirates who think families are easy prey. We have collectors who want the Reckoning. And we have {enemy}, whose gate wardens think a people with a map of their own is a people with ideas. Fly well, Captain."
      ],
      "outro": [
        "The {base} holds, {captain}, and the fleet is whole.\n\nSabra: Dov has read the next gate in the Reckoning. It's a sleeping gate, out past the Shroud Arm. It hasn't opened for anyone in living memory.\n\nDov: Not yet.\n\nSabra: That's what he always says. That's what his father always said. One day one of them will be right.\n\nKit: You've a Sunbird and a berth here whenever you want them. That's not nothing. To us it's most things.",
        "It's done. {enemy} has withdrawn its order, for now, and the Synod has written a very long letter about it.\n\nSabra: We'll move on soon. The {base} doesn't stay anywhere long.\n\nDov: I've written your name in the Reckoning, Captain. In the margin, mind. The margin is for friends."
      ],
      "briefing-wing": [
        "Sabra: First flight, Captain. Two of our family ships are holding near the {base} while they mend a drive. Raiders have been sniffing about. Fly with Kit and keep them off.\n\nKit: Sunbirds turn faster than anything those raiders fly. Use it.",
        "Sabra: Family ships are sitting out in {system} waiting on repairs. Raiders are coming. Guard them.\n\nKit: Stay close to me and closer to the families."
